    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# RLHF: Reward Model + PPO Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: Synthetic Preference Data"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "In production, human annotators create preference data. We'll create synthetic pairs where the \"preferred\" response is objectively better (more concise, more accurate, more helpful)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import numpy as np"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "PREFERENCE_DATA = ["
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    {"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"prompt\": \"What is the capital of France?\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"preferred\": \"The capital of France is Paris.\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"rejected\": \"France is a country in Europe. It has many cities. The capital is Paris. Paris is known for the Eiffel Tower.\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    },"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    {"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"prompt\": \"Explain gravity in one sentence.\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"preferred\": \"Gravity is the force that attracts objects with mass toward each other.\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"rejected\": \"Gravity is something that makes things fall down when you drop them.\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    },"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    {"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"prompt\": \"What is 15 times 7?\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"preferred\": \"15 times 7 is 105.\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"rejected\": \"Let me think about this. 15 times 7. Well, 10 times 7 is 70, and 5 times 7 is 35, so the answer might be around 105.\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    },"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    {"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"prompt\": \"Name three programming languages.\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"preferred\": \"Python, Rust, and TypeScript.\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"rejected\": \"There are many programming languages. Some popular ones include various languages like Python and others.\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    },"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    {"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"prompt\": \"What year did World War II end?\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"preferred\": \"World War II ended in 1945.\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"rejected\": \"World War II was a major global conflict. It involved many countries. The war ended in the mid-1940s, specifically in 1945.\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    },"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    {"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"prompt\": \"Define machine learning.\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"preferred\": \"Machine learning is a field where algorithms learn patterns from data to make predictions without being explicitly programmed.\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"rejected\": \"Machine learning is a type of AI. AI stands for artificial intelligence. Machine learning uses data to learn.\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    },"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The preferred responses are concise and direct. The rejected responses exhibit common failure modes: unnecessary padding, hedging, redundant explanation, and imprecision. This is exactly the kind of distinction that SFT cannot capture but RLHF can."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: Reward Model Architecture"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The reward model reuses the transformer architecture from the mini GPT, but replaces the vocabulary-sized output head with a single scalar projection."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import sys"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import os"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "sys.path.insert(0, os.path.join(os.path.dirname(__file__), \"..\", \"..\", \"04-pre-training-mini-gpt\", \"code\"))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from main import MiniGPT, LayerNorm, Embedding, TransformerBlock"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class RewardModel:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, vocab_size=256, embed_dim=128, num_heads=4,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                 num_layers=4, max_seq_len=128, ff_dim=512):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.embedding = Embedding(vocab_size, embed_dim, max_seq_len)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.blocks = ["
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            TransformerBlock(embed_dim, num_heads, ff_dim)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            for _ in range(num_layers)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        ]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.ln_f = LayerNorm(embed_dim)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.reward_head = np.random.randn(embed_dim) * 0.02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def forward(self, token_ids):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        seq_len = token_ids.shape[-1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        mask = np.triu(np.full((seq_len, seq_len), -1e9), k=1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x = self.embedding.forward(token_ids)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for block in self.blocks:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            x = block.forward(x, mask)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x = self.ln_f.forward(x)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        last_hidden = x[:, -1, :]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        reward = last_hidden @ self.reward_head"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return reward"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The reward model takes the hidden state at the *last* token position and projects it to a scalar. Why the last token? Because the causal attention mask means the last position has attended to every previous token. It has the most complete representation of the entire (prompt, response) sequence."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: Bradley-Terry Loss"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Train the reward model on preference pairs using the Bradley-Terry pairwise loss."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def tokenize_for_reward(prompt, response, vocab_size=256):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    prompt_tokens = [min(t, vocab_size - 1) for t in list(prompt.encode(\"utf-8\"))]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    response_tokens = [min(t, vocab_size - 1) for t in list(response.encode(\"utf-8\"))]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return prompt_tokens + [0] + response_tokens"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def sigmoid(x):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return np.where("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x >= 0,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        1.0 / (1.0 + np.exp(-x)),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        np.exp(x) / (1.0 + np.exp(x))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    )"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def bradley_terry_loss(reward_preferred, reward_rejected):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    diff = reward_preferred - reward_rejected"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    loss = -np.log(sigmoid(diff) + 1e-8)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return loss"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def train_reward_model(rm, preference_data, num_epochs=10, lr=1e-4, max_seq_len=128):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(f\"Training Reward Model: {len(preference_data)} preference pairs, {num_epochs} epochs\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    losses = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    accuracies = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for epoch in range(num_epochs):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        epoch_loss = 0.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        epoch_correct = 0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        num_pairs = 0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        indices = np.random.permutation(len(preference_data))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for idx in indices:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            pair = preference_data[idx]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            preferred_tokens = tokenize_for_reward(pair[\"prompt\"], pair[\"preferred\"])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            rejected_tokens = tokenize_for_reward(pair[\"prompt\"], pair[\"rejected\"])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            preferred_tokens = preferred_tokens[:max_seq_len]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            rejected_tokens = rejected_tokens[:max_seq_len]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            preferred_ids = np.array(preferred_tokens).reshape(1, -1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            rejected_ids = np.array(rejected_tokens).reshape(1, -1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            r_preferred = rm.forward(preferred_ids)[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            r_rejected = rm.forward(rejected_ids)[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            loss = bradley_terry_loss(r_preferred, r_rejected)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            if r_preferred > r_rejected:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                epoch_correct += 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            diff = r_preferred - r_rejected"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            grad = sigmoid(diff) - 1.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            rm.reward_head -= lr * grad * rm.ln_f.forward("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                rm.embedding.forward(preferred_ids)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            )[:, -1, :].flatten()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            epoch_loss += loss"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            num_pairs += 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        avg_loss = epoch_loss / max(num_pairs, 1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        accuracy = epoch_correct / max(num_pairs, 1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        losses.append(avg_loss)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        accuracies.append(accuracy)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if epoch % 2 == 0:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            print(f\"  Epoch {epoch + 1:3d} | Loss: {avg_loss:.4f} | Accuracy: {accuracy:.1%}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return rm, losses, accuracies"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The accuracy metric is straightforward: what fraction of preference pairs does the reward model rank correctly? A random model scores 50%. A well-trained reward model on clean data should exceed 70%. InstructGPT's reward model achieved about 72% accuracy on held-out comparisons, which sounds low but is actually good -- many preference pairs are ambiguous even to humans (inter-annotator agreement was about 73%)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: Simplified PPO Loop"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Full PPO is complex. This implementation captures the core mechanism: generate responses, score them, compute the advantage, and update the policy with a KL penalty."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def compute_kl_divergence(policy_logits, reference_logits):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    policy_probs = np.exp(policy_logits - policy_logits.max(axis=-1, keepdims=True))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    policy_probs = policy_probs / policy_probs.sum(axis=-1, keepdims=True)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    policy_probs = np.clip(policy_probs, 1e-10, 1.0)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    ref_probs = np.exp(reference_logits - reference_logits.max(axis=-1, keepdims=True))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    ref_probs = ref_probs / ref_probs.sum(axis=-1, keepdims=True)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    ref_probs = np.clip(ref_probs, 1e-10, 1.0)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    kl = np.sum(policy_probs * np.log(policy_probs / ref_probs), axis=-1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return kl.mean()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def generate_response(model, prompt_tokens, max_new_tokens=30, temperature=0.8, max_seq_len=128):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    tokens = list(prompt_tokens)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for _ in range(max_new_tokens):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        context = np.array(tokens[-max_seq_len:]).reshape(1, -1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        logits = model.forward(context)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        next_logits = logits[0, -1, :]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        next_logits = next_logits / max(temperature, 1e-8)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        probs = np.exp(next_logits - next_logits.max())"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        probs = probs / probs.sum()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        probs = np.clip(probs, 1e-10, 1.0)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        probs = probs / probs.sum()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        next_token = np.random.choice(len(probs), p=probs)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        tokens.append(int(next_token))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return tokens"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def copy_model_weights(source, target):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    target.embedding.token_embed = source.embedding.token_embed.copy()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    target.embedding.pos_embed = source.embedding.pos_embed.copy()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    target.ln_f.gamma = source.ln_f.gamma.copy()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    target.ln_f.beta = source.ln_f.beta.copy()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for s_block, t_block in zip(source.blocks, target.blocks):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        t_block.attn.W_q = s_block.attn.W_q.copy()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        t_block.attn.W_k = s_block.attn.W_k.copy()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        t_block.attn.W_v = s_block.attn.W_v.copy()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        t_block.attn.W_out = s_block.attn.W_out.copy()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        t_block.ffn.W1 = s_block.ffn.W1.copy()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        t_block.ffn.W2 = s_block.ffn.W2.copy()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        t_block.ffn.b1 = s_block.ffn.b1.copy()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        t_block.ffn.b2 = s_block.ffn.b2.copy()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        t_block.ln1.gamma = s_block.ln1.gamma.copy()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        t_block.ln1.beta = s_block.ln1.beta.copy()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        t_block.ln2.gamma = s_block.ln2.gamma.copy()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        t_block.ln2.beta = s_block.ln2.beta.copy()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def ppo_training(policy_model, reference_model, reward_model, prompts,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                 num_episodes=20, lr=1.5e-5, kl_coeff=0.02, max_seq_len=128):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(f\"PPO Training: {num_episodes} episodes, lr={lr}, KL coeff={kl_coeff}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    rewards_history = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    kl_history = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for episode in range(num_episodes):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        prompt_text = prompts[episode % len(prompts)]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        prompt_tokens = [min(t, 252) for t in list(prompt_text.encode(\"utf-8\"))]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        response_tokens = generate_response("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            policy_model, prompt_tokens,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            max_new_tokens=20, temperature=0.8, max_seq_len=max_seq_len"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        )"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        response_ids = np.array(response_tokens[:max_seq_len]).reshape(1, -1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        reward = reward_model.forward(response_ids)[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        policy_logits = policy_model.forward(response_ids)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        ref_logits = reference_model.forward(response_ids)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        kl = compute_kl_divergence(policy_logits, ref_logits)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        total_reward = reward - kl_coeff * kl"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        rewards_history.append(float(reward))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        kl_history.append(float(kl))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for block in policy_model.blocks:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            update_scale = lr * total_reward"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            block.ffn.W1 += update_scale * np.random.randn(*block.ffn.W1.shape) * 0.01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            block.ffn.W2 += update_scale * np.random.randn(*block.ffn.W2.shape) * 0.01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if episode % 5 == 0:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            avg_reward = np.mean(rewards_history[-5:]) if rewards_history else 0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            avg_kl = np.mean(kl_history[-5:]) if kl_history else 0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            print(f\"  Episode {episode:3d} | Reward: {reward:.4f} | KL: {kl:.4f} | \""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                  f\"Avg Reward: {avg_reward:.4f}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return policy_model, rewards_history, kl_history"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The core loop: (1) sample a prompt, (2) generate a response, (3) score it with the reward model, (4) compute KL divergence against the frozen reference, (5) compute the adjusted reward (reward minus KL penalty), (6) update the policy. The KL penalty grows as the policy diverges from the reference, automatically preventing reward hacking."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 5: Reward Score Comparison"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "After RLHF, the policy model's responses should score higher on the reward model than the original SFT model's responses."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def compare_models(sft_model, rlhf_model, reward_model, prompts, max_seq_len=128):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(\"Model Comparison (reward scores)\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(\"-\" * 60)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(f\"  {'Prompt':<35} {'SFT':>10} {'RLHF':>10}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(\"  \" + \"-\" * 55)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    sft_total = 0.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    rlhf_total = 0.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for prompt in prompts:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        prompt_tokens = [min(t, 252) for t in list(prompt.encode(\"utf-8\"))]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        sft_response = generate_response("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            sft_model, prompt_tokens,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            max_new_tokens=20, temperature=0.6, max_seq_len=max_seq_len"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        )"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        rlhf_response = generate_response("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            rlhf_model, prompt_tokens,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            max_new_tokens=20, temperature=0.6, max_seq_len=max_seq_len"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        )"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        sft_ids = np.array(sft_response[:max_seq_len]).reshape(1, -1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        rlhf_ids = np.array(rlhf_response[:max_seq_len]).reshape(1, -1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        sft_reward = reward_model.forward(sft_ids)[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        rlhf_reward = reward_model.forward(rlhf_ids)[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        sft_total += sft_reward"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        rlhf_total += rlhf_reward"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        truncated_prompt = prompt[:33] + \"..\" if len(prompt) > 35 else prompt"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        print(f\"  {truncated_prompt:<35} {sft_reward:>10.4f} {rlhf_reward:>10.4f}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    n = len(prompts)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(\"  \" + \"-\" * 55)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(f\"  {'Average':<35} {sft_total/n:>10.4f} {rlhf_total/n:>10.4f}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return sft_total / n, rlhf_total / n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
